A||N||3||jscott1||Power door lock actuators||||5||
Z||000000||jscott1||12-01-2001||01:58 AM||||I just bought an 88 coupe with no power options, and now I am adding power door locks using individual original parts,(no donor car).  <P>I have the factory service manual, (Helms) so I know how to wire everything, but there does not appear to be anywhere to physically mount door lock actuators and even if there were there is nothing to connect them to.  The mechanism shown in the manual is missing from my door.  <P>The factor actuators appear to move in a vertical fashion and a right angle piece changes that to a back and forth motion which actually unlocks the door.  The right angle peice is nowhere to be found in my door.  There is just a long metal rod going from the interior door lock back to the door lock mechanism.<P>I have been lurking in this forum for months and no one has yet mentioned this fact.  Does anybody out there know exactly how to mount the actuators in a door that originally did not have them? <P>- Jonathan ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||12-01-2001||02:10 AM||||There's a bracket that the right angle piece is mounted to.  It's riveted to the door inner and spans the gap vertically where the door linkage makes the short jog.  That's where the right angle bracket drives the linkage.  <P>The actuators can be bolted in using short bolts (short enough to clear the glass when rolled down).  I believe all of the mounting holes are stamped in all doors.  I've done the swap and I didn't have to do any cutting or drilling.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||12-01-2001||02:13 AM||||Yes.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oh, you wanted me to tell you?!  Ok...  heh...<P>The factory door locks are the biggest PITA to get in and out, you're FAAAAAR better off with aftermarkets.<P>As they say, a picture says a thousand words, so here:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/doorlock1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/doorlock2.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jscott1||12-01-2001||02:29 AM||||thanks for the tip Watts.  Since I don't have a right angle bracket I am going to have to use an aftermarket type installation.  I wish I had known that before I wasted my money on the Fiero actuators. <p>[This message has been edited by jscott1 (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
